// ============================================================
// QUERY: Power Automate Mail Forward API Detection
// Incident: INC-2026-87241
// Table: MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
// Purpose: Detect automated email forwarding via the Graph API
//          /forward endpoint, executed by Power Automate service
//          principals. This is a persistence and exfiltration
//          technique that survives password reset.
// Platform: Microsoft Sentinel
// ============================================================

MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
| where RequestUri contains "/forward"
| where ResponseStatusCode == 202
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(24h)
| project TimeGenerated, RequestUri, IPAddress

// ============================================================
// INCIDENT CONTEXT:
//   - Compromised User:       m.smith@lognpacific.org
//   - Flow Created:           2026-06-10 23:05:05 UTC
//   - Forward Executed:       2026-06-11 07:41:09 UTC (9+ hrs after breach)
//   - Execution IP:           20.150.129.194 (Microsoft O365 datacenter — NOT attacker)
//   - Service Principal:      7ab7862c-4c57-491e-8a45-d52a7e023983 (Power Automate)
//   - Response Code:          202 (Accepted)
//   - Exfiltration Target:    merovingian1337@proton.me
//   - Email Subject Forwarded: "FW: Updated Banking Details - Pacific IT Monthly"
//
// WHY THIS IS DANGEROUS:
//   1. Attacker does NOT need to be logged in — flow runs automatically
//   2. Source IP is Microsoft infrastructure — looks like legitimate mail
//   3. Survives password reset — runs as service principal, not user
//   4. Captures ALL future emails — incident response comms, credential resets
//   5. Hard to detect — not a user action, requires MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs
//
// DETECTION SEQUENCE (two-table correlation):
//   - MicrosoftGraphActivityLogs: POST /forward API call (202 Accepted)
//   - OfficeActivity: Resulting Send operation recorded moments later
//   The Graph call fires FIRST, then OfficeActivity captures the mail event.
//   Correlate these two events to confirm automated forwarding.
//
// COMPANION QUERY — Detect Power Automate Flow Creation:
//
//   CloudAppEvents
//   | where ActionType == "CreateFlow"
//   | where Timestamp >= ago(7d)
//   | project Timestamp, AccountObjectId, ActionType, ObjectName
//
// TUNING:
//   - Alert on /forward API calls from service principals (not user accounts)
//   - Alert on /forward API calls where target is external email domain
//   - Correlate CreateFlow events with subsequent /forward API calls
//   - Monitor Power Automate Admin Center for unexpected cloud flows
//   - AppId 7ab7862c-4c57-491e-8a45-d52a7e023983 = Power Automate service principal
// ============================================================
